															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mark-penrice" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1858819); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1858819&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606401735" alt="Mark Penrice" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1858819)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mark-penrice" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1858819); return false;" >Mark Penrice</a></span> <span class="odate time_1546721354 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 Jan 2019 20:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4109649">
									

<p>Thanks for doing that, because I don't think I'd fully grasped it at first. It's actually so difficult to understand - a good thing in this particular context! - that the true nature of it wasn't entirely clear.</p>
<p>I figured it as (no spoilers here, btw) something that was universally cognitohazardous regardless of how you perceived it, even if just via ambient sound echoes or haptic vibration/touch through your hands or even soles of your feet. So all of those senses had to be extremely well-filtered and damped whilst triangulating the actual location of the anomaly and building some kind of container around it (*hopefully* it's a static object&#8230;), and even whilst in the box there's the potential for leakage.</p>
<p>So now the Foundation know they've got *something* deadly locked up, but they don't know what it is, or even if it'll stay there (presumably it not having escaped *yet* is why it's Euclid rather than Keter), and it's dangerous even for unprepared D-class to remain too close to because just by seeing the box they pick up some information about e.g. its position and maximum possible size&#8230;</p>
Somewhat spoilery:
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Headcanon is that it's something that the lone toddler made during a cookie-cooking class in the kitchen, whilst being REALLY bad at making cookies but unexpectedly good at creating anart-type objects, and it's only their general obliviousness* (given their age) which protected them from the effects, at least at first&#8230;</p>
<ul>
<li>Or more correctly their general incompetence at everything, including noticing what it is they've made and paying attention to it. It's a rather odd thing that being good at a job related to the object, including knowing anything about it, would cause you to bleed out from the head, but presumably it invokes some kind of fractal restructuring of the part of the brain responsible for memory and procedure&#8230;</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>

