					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aismallard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4598089); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4598089&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606401735" alt="aismallard" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4598089)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aismallard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4598089); return false;" >aismallard</a></span> <span class="odate time_1546460424 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Jan 2019 20:20</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4106407">
									

<p>For <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/cliche-con-2019">Cliché-Con 2019</a>, in <span style="text-decoration: underline;">Category 2 - Article features a cliché story element</span>.<br />
<span style="text-decoration: underline;">Clichés</span>:</p>
<ul>
<li>A highly skilled Mobile Task Force gets steamrolled.</li>
<li>D-Class = Disposable Class</li>
</ul>
<p>Thanks to wctaiwan, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4187885); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187885&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1549347926" alt="Rounderhouse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187885)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4187885); return false;">Rounderhouse</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ensophos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1676981); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1676981&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1549347926" alt="Ensophos" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1676981)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ensophos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1676981); return false;">Ensophos</a></span> for critiques.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It's an infohazard that reverses &quot;competent&quot; and &quot;incompetent&quot; whenever you work with information about it. As evident in the recovery, being too knowledgable about it (a form of competence) is fatal.</p>
<p>As such, the D-class who attend to it must be very unable to handle it normally, be unable to improve their skill at containing it, and cannot communicate anything substantial about it to the outside world.</p>
<p>What the object actually is is unstated, and is not knowable in-universe.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>There is now also a <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/SCPDeclassified/comments/anbeco/scp3597_maladroit/">declassification</a>! (also spoilers)</p>

